WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.883 --> 00:00:04.794
- [Voiceover] Any shoe
you need, I probably have.

00:00:04.794 --> 00:00:08.421
If I don't have it, I can
get it for you in 24 hours.

00:00:08.421 --> 00:00:10.668
If you're a rapper and
you have a video shoot,

00:00:10.668 --> 00:00:13.220
and you need the shoes
coming out in two weeks,

00:00:13.220 --> 00:00:17.387
I just have to make a call,
and I'll get it for you.

00:00:24.449 --> 00:00:26.005
- [Voiceover] Everyday millions of people

00:00:26.005 --> 00:00:28.487
tune to DJ Khaled's Snapchat.

00:00:28.487 --> 00:00:31.780
- The key to more success
is to have a lot of pillows.

00:00:31.780 --> 00:00:32.743
- [Voiceover] One of my favorite

00:00:32.743 --> 00:00:35.005
DJ Khaled appearances is this kid.

00:00:35.005 --> 00:00:36.716
- [Khaled] Ben, how's
business in the new year?

00:00:36.716 --> 00:00:38.097
- Booming.

00:00:38.097 --> 00:00:39.302
- [Khaled] I see you.

00:00:39.302 --> 00:00:41.070
- [Voiceover] He's 16 years
old and he's at the helm

00:00:41.070 --> 00:00:42.983
burgeoning sneaker empire.

00:00:42.983 --> 00:00:44.910
One that he says has done
nearly a million dollars

00:00:44.910 --> 00:00:46.617
in business and boasts clients

00:00:46.617 --> 00:00:48.786
like DJ Khaled and Chris Brown.

00:00:48.786 --> 00:00:49.958
- Are you at the studio?

00:00:49.958 --> 00:00:51.817
- [Voiceover] Meet the Sneaker Don.

00:00:51.817 --> 00:00:53.610
- So, my name is Benjamin Kapelushnik,

00:00:53.610 --> 00:00:54.919
people call me Benjamin Kicks,

00:00:54.919 --> 00:00:58.661
but most of you guys know
me as the Sneaker Don.

00:00:58.661 --> 00:01:01.546
School ends at three o'clock
and I get home at, like, four.

00:01:01.546 --> 00:01:03.180
I eat dinner, do some homework,

00:01:03.180 --> 00:01:05.916
and go straight to the office space.

00:01:05.916 --> 00:01:08.769
- [Voiceover] And like any
good don, family's important.

00:01:08.769 --> 00:01:10.384
- I'm Ben's littlest brother.

00:01:10.384 --> 00:01:13.545
I'm his manager, so if you
need anything, call me.

00:01:13.545 --> 00:01:14.758
- [Voiceover] Okay, not that family.

00:01:14.758 --> 00:01:16.815
- I'm the mother of the Sneaker Don.

00:01:16.815 --> 00:01:20.539
To me, he's my little boy,
but I also see a businessman.

00:01:20.539 --> 00:01:22.826
He had a goal, he's self-driven,

00:01:22.826 --> 00:01:25.743
he's motivated, he's a hard worker.

00:01:26.649 --> 00:01:28.708
- [Voiceover] The great dons, they say,

00:01:28.708 --> 00:01:31.114
come from humble beginnings.

00:01:31.114 --> 00:01:32.358
- [Benjamin] The first
pair of sneakers that

00:01:32.358 --> 00:01:34.036
actually got me in the sneaker game,

00:01:34.036 --> 00:01:37.246
I was in fifth grade,
the galaxy pack came out,

00:01:37.246 --> 00:01:39.570
and I got the Lebrons.

00:01:39.570 --> 00:01:41.063
I loved sneakers after that.

00:01:41.063 --> 00:01:42.823
Probably around sixth
grade when my parents

00:01:42.823 --> 00:01:44.589
didn't want to fund my
sneaker hobby anymore

00:01:44.589 --> 00:01:46.744
I had to figure out a way
how to get the money for it.

00:01:46.744 --> 00:01:50.173
And then I realized if
I buy five or ten pairs

00:01:50.173 --> 00:01:52.315
by paying people to stand in line for me,

00:01:52.315 --> 00:01:54.504
I could sell it to a larger clientele

00:01:54.504 --> 00:01:58.030
and make more money, plus
get my shoes for free.

00:01:58.030 --> 00:02:00.460
And then it just finally broke through

00:02:00.460 --> 00:02:02.363
and money just started coming in.

00:02:02.363 --> 00:02:04.675
At first it amazed me how
sneakers can go for, like,

00:02:04.675 --> 00:02:06.135
so much money for like one
shoe people are charging

00:02:06.135 --> 00:02:08.409
a thousand and I thought it
was a, like, joke or something.

00:02:08.409 --> 00:02:11.466
- [Voiceover] $1,000? But hey that's why

00:02:11.466 --> 00:02:13.216
he's the Sneaker Don.

00:02:14.363 --> 00:02:16.030
So, what comes next?

00:02:17.229 --> 00:02:19.752
- [Benjamin] Really excited
to open up a physical store.

00:02:19.752 --> 00:02:21.429
The first location is gonna be Miami,

00:02:21.429 --> 00:02:24.240
and then I'm trying to do
L.A., New York, and Chicago.

00:02:24.240 --> 00:02:26.139
All my friends, when they
dropped out of the sneaker game

00:02:26.139 --> 00:02:27.742
they're like "It's dead, it's over,

00:02:27.742 --> 00:02:28.840
there's no more, like,
you're not doing anything,

00:02:28.840 --> 00:02:31.399
you're wasting your time,
you're gonna lose money."

00:02:31.399 --> 00:02:33.259
None of the above was true.

00:02:33.259 --> 00:02:34.752
Played themselves.

00:02:34.752 --> 00:02:38.166
- [Voiceover] Indeed they did,
Sneaker Don. Indeed they did.

00:02:38.166 --> 00:02:40.749
(upbeat music)

